### An exact decimal target

The half-degree step is validated relative to the minimum. Entering a value such as 20.2 does not silently round the draft or move the thumb to a different value.

<%= example('slider-temperature') %>

### A signed value

Zero and negative values are valid in this invented display-offset range. Neither signifies an unknown reading. A text field preserves access to a minus sign on mobile keyboards.

<%= example('slider-signed-offset') %>

### A failed request

The earlier reported value stays at 25%. The retained 40% draft is clearly a proposed change. Repeating this local preview demonstrates a failure response without issuing a command.

<%= example('slider-request-failed') %>

### An unavailable device

A range input always has a numeric position. Hide the editable range when no usable value is available instead of presenting its minimum or midpoint as a measurement. Keep the device name, reason and details route.

